Aerie-Purpose: Seed Helium's audio jitter (rendered AudioBuffers and AnalyserNode readbacks) from the site and session noise token and the sample coordinates only, so a repeated render or read gives the same bytes and a tracker cannot average the noise away.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webaudio/audio_buffer.cc (AudioBuffer::JitterAudioData), third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webaudio/realtime_analyser.cc (AudioAnalyzerNoiseState)

Amends helium-chromium/patches/helium/core/noise/audio.patch (issue #38). That patch xors
a process-wide base::AtomicSequenceNumber into the coordinate seed of every rendered
buffer (g_helium_audio_render_sequence) and of every analyser read
(g_helium_audio_analyzer_read_sequence), so each render or read of the same graph on the
same site got different noise. Canvas noise is stable per site per session, which is the
stronger design. This patch drops both counters. The seed is now the channel (high bits) and
the frame index for buffers, and the per-method domain constant and the index for analyser
reads. BaseAudioContext::JitterAudioData mixes it with the per-site, per-session kAudio
token and the sample bits. The noise strength, the kHeliumNoiseAudio feature switch and the
per-site noise control (the token is absent when noise is off) are untouched.

